\section{Restart}{

Every output is written under a temporary name and renamed into place once
complete, so an output file is either absent or whole, and a batch is done
when its output exists. With \code{resume = TRUE} (the default), a re-run:
\enumerate{
\item removes temporary files left by a crash;
\item reads the ledger, and marks as \code{"interrupted"} every batch whose last
event is \code{"started"} by a process that no longer exists (a shutdown,
a crash, or a killed session);
\item skips batches whose outputs exist, and batches still running in another
live process;
\item re-runs the rest: never-started, interrupted and (with
\code{retry_failed = TRUE}) failed batches.
}

So after any interruption, call the function again with the same arguments.
\code{\link[=batch_status]{batch_status()}} shows where a run stands without starting anything.
With \code{"profile"} in \code{steps} and an existing emp-map, only the profile is
built, from the emp-map and the batch file; the linkage is not repeated.
}

